WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.160
This summer, the superhero world will face
the end of an era one that doesn't have anything

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.120
to do with the Avengers.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.700
Fox's X-Men series is finally coming to a
close with an adaptation of an iconic Marvel

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.509
story: Dark Phoenix.

00:00:14.509 --> 00:00:19.700
Here are a few of the things you need to know
before you see the last of the X-Men movies.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.380
And there are spoilers ahead!

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.990
But it's spoilers from the trailer.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.080
Regardless, be forewarned!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.900
The beginnings of a saga

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.650
The Dark Phoenix Saga, as it's come to be
known through years of reprints and adaptations,

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.070
is perhaps the most famous and widely referenced
storyline in the history of X-Men comics though

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.270
it has often been taken very loosely when
adapted to the screen.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:46.690
The setup for the story began in Uncanny X-Men
#101 in 1976, with the X-Men embarking on

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.610
a mission to space, during which Jean Grey
encounters what seems to be a deadly solar

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.610
flare.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:57.770
In that moment, instead of dying, she reaches
the full potential of her Omega-level mutant

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.370
powers, which allow her to transcend her corporeal
form.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:06.200
Jean later returns to her body, though when
she reunites with the X-Men she has a new

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.149
look, a greatly enhanced set of powers, and
the name "Phoenix."

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:15.590
For a while, this became somewhat of a status
quo in the X-Men comics, as Phoenix seemed

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:20.170
to be able to hold back her own darker urges
and maintain a power level that allowed her

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.259
to remain a valuable ally to the X-Men.

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:24.950
But that wouldn't last for long.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:25.950
Evil

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:31.110
The Dark Phoenix saga proper was kicked off
three years later in Uncanny X-Men #129, when

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.319
creators Chris Claremont and John Byrne decided
it was time to truly activate Jean Grey's

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:41.750
full potential, not just as an incredibly
powerful being, but as a supervillain.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:46.569
This begins with the evil mutant Mastermind
dominating Jean's mind, projecting visions

00:01:46.569 --> 00:01:51.149
into her head that eventually lead her to
assume the evil identity of "The Black Queen"

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:52.890
and rebel against the X-Men.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.759
Jean briefly joins the Hellfire Club before
realizing the deception that put her there,

00:01:57.759 --> 00:02:02.539
strikes down Mastermind, and then eventually
chooses to abandon all ties to her former

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.630
identity as "Jean Grey."

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:09.140
Phoenix defeats the X-Men and takes to space,
but her journey through the cosmos leaves

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:14.720
her so drained that she consumes an entire
solar system to restore her power, inadvertently

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.930
causing mass genocide on nearby planets.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:23.159
A council of cosmic leaders then determine
that Phoenix is a threat greater than even

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:25.770
Galactus and must be put down.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:30.810
Meanwhile, Jean has returned home, where the
X-Men work to restore her "Jean Grey" identity.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.940
They seem to succeed, but the universe demands
a price be paid.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.940
The last stand

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.599
Though the X-Men are able to bring Jean's
original personality to the forefront once

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:44.270
again, there had to be consequences for Phoenix's
trail of destruction.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:49.090
The Shi'ar empress Lilandra orders her Imperial
Guard a group of the best fighters in the

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.010
galaxy to abduct the X-Men and put Phoenix
to death.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:58.670
Charles Xavier instead challenges the Shi'ar
to a trial by combat: the X-Men versus the

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.109
Imperial Guard, with the fate of the Phoenix
at stake.

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:06.680
A lengthy battle ensues on the Blue Area of
the Moon, but the Imperial Guard eventually

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.409
defeat the X-Men.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:13.230
In the chaos, Jean struggles to keep control
as the Dark Phoenix fights to overwhelm her

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.079
body once again.

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:19.890
Before this can happen, she uses a piece of
alien machinery to kill herself after professing

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.409
her love for Cyclops.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:26.470
Jean Grey has come back from the dead more
than once since this saga ended, but its impact

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.650
remains clear among X-Men fans and within
X-Men continuity.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.980
Jean Grey's struggle to retain her humanity
even while tempted by the godlike powers within

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:41.870
her remains one of the most emotionally satisfying
and gripping X-Men stories, and now a real

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.819
adaptation of it is finally coming to the
big screen.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:45.840
Where we're at

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.830
Dark Phoenix will complete the saga of films
that began with X-Men: First Class and continued

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.799
through Days of Future Past and Apocalypse.

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:57.780
Each of these films took the team through
a different decade of Earth's history, with

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:03.180
Dark Phoenix finally landing the X-Men in
the 1990s, at a time when Charles Xavier and

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.150
his adoptive sister Mystique are leading a
new team of X-Men.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:12.650
This team includes mainstays such as Cyclops,
as well as the star of the movie: Jean Grey.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.060
The chief consequence of Apocalypse that the
film will be dealing with is no doubt Jean's

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:21.980
understanding of her own powers, which she
finally unleashed at the end of the last film,

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:25.760
as the only way to stop the evil mutant En
Sabah Nur.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.290
Jean held nothing back, and although it led
to victory for the X-Men, it also released

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.840
something frightening.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.130
Dark Phoenix will see those powers enhanced
by a mission to space that will bring her

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:40.960
into contact with the film's version of the
Phoenix Force, a mysterious cosmic entity

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.170
that greatly increases her powers.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.170
Lingering questions

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:48.450
Jean will be the driving force of Dark Phoenix,
but she's far from the only major character

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.490
left over from Apocalypse.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:56.030
The team at the X-Mansion now includes a reformed
Ororo Munroe, also known as Storm, as well

00:04:56.030 --> 00:05:00.290
as the speedster mutant Quicksilver and the
teleporter Nightcrawler.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.480
Based on what can be gleaned from the trailers,
this team seems to be in relatively stable

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:09.140
shape as the film begins, with Xavier and
senior members Mystique and Beast leading

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.360
the way for the younger crew.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.940
There's another mutant element at work in
the wake of Apocalypse, though, and that's

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.260
Magneto.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:20.870
Erik Lehnsherr allowed himself to be drawn
in by En Sabah Nur's power, thinking he could

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:25.680
use it as a means to make the world anew for
mutantkind, but he was ultimately repulsed

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.640
by the senseless destruction and helped the
X-Men to defeat him.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:34.120
Now, after helping to rebuild in the wake
of Apocalypse, he's started his own little

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.790
mutant community.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.660
There are bigger questions hanging over all
of this, of course, beyond the allegiances

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.880
of individual mutant characters.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.430
How has the world changed since Apocalypse?

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.550
Who is still feeling the trauma of the events
of that film?

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.240
And how will they bring those emotions into
this new conflict?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.240
The end of an era

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.690
If Dark Phoenix had stuck to its original
release date of fall 2018, there might have

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:59.840
been room to speculate on exactly how the
team will continue after the events of the

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.840
film.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.900
But things are a little bit different now.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.280
After Dark Phoenix entered production in the
fall of 2017, the Walt Disney Company made

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.670
a move to merge with 21st Century Fox, the
media corporation which includes 20th Century

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:18.610
Fox the film studio which produced the X-Men
series, among many other movies and TV shows.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:22.070
The merger process was completed in March
2019.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:27.610
As a result, Disney has taken now over ownership
of most of Fox's media properties including

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.920
the X-Men.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:34.430
Now, Dark Phoenix is one of two mutant films
left as holdovers from the old Fox regime.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:39.690
With that in mind, speculation has been rampant
over just what will become of these X-Men.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:45.040
Is it over for them, or will they find new
life one day in the Marvel Cinematic Universe?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:50.230
According to Fox executive Emma Watts, Dark
Phoenix will be a, quote, "perfect send-off"

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:55.060
to the X-Men team Fox has built for the last
two decades, signaling to fans everywhere

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.870
that this will indeed be their last ride.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:00.500
In that sense, it really is the end of an
era.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.500
Early days

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.450
Though fans are now getting a film that not
only bears the title Dark Phoenix, but seems

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:09.960
fully intent on adapting the story for the
screen, it's not the first time filmmakers

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.450
have turned their eyes toward such a project.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:17.220
The first trilogy of X-Men films actually
carried out its own version of the Dark Phoenix

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.900
story, though in a much different way, with
Jean Grey seemingly perishing at the end of

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:28.080
X2: X-Men United and returning as a force
of destruction in X-Men: The Last Stand.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.970
But screenwriter Zak Penn, who has a story
credit on X2, has told The Hollywood Reporter

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:38.720
that what fans almost got was a direct Dark
Phoenix Saga adaptation for X2, which he pushed

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.570
against for fear that the film was going too
far, too early in the franchise.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.570
Penn explained:

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:48.850
"It was too soon to go into the Phoenix story
and it was too soon to get cosmic.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:53.530
I would say that's probably the biggest contribution
I made was pushing it in that direction."

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:59.180
Instead, X2 ended up merely hinting at Dark
Phoenix, and ended up doing its own version

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:04.460
of the classic X-Men comics story God Loves,
Man Kills, in which the team must stop a plot

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.600
by William Stryker to eradicate mutants from
the Earth.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.600
Delays

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:13.070
Dark Phoenix was originally set to be released
in November of 2018 before that release date

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.670
was dropped in favor of Valentine's Day, 2019.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:21.350
In September of last year, Fox announced that
they'd moved the release date again, this

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.700
time setting the film for its current date
of June 7.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.760
So, what happened with the delays?

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:32.200
According to director Simon Kinberg, a number
of different factors led to the film's pushed-back

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.200
release.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.710
The final delay came when visual effects delays
on Dark Phoenix coincided with the Gambit

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.270
movie sliding out of its summer spot.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.270
Kinberg explained:

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:46.720
"We looked at that date versus the February
14th date, the studio did and we did, we felt

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.180
like that June date was a bigger opportunity
for us globally.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:54.360
More screens, more IMAX screens, a better
chance to play in China…

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:58.640
Specific for us, it is an opportunity to be
a bigger movie day-and-date globally."

00:08:58.640 --> 00:08:59.640
Genosha

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.090
In the Dark Phoenix trailers, it's possible
to see glimpses of Magneto and Jean spending

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:09.300
time in what looks like a kind of jungle commune,
with makeshift structures and sparse signs

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.680
of civilization.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:15.890
According to Kinberg, this is an early version
of Genosha, one of the most important locations

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:20.380
in the X-Men comics, and a key part of Magneto's
history.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:24.620
Originally introduced as a kind of mutant
apartheid state, the nation eventually becomes

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:29.130
Magneto's domain, and in the film it will
serve as a place where he can attempt to create

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.500
a promised land for mutantkind.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.590
Kinberg explains:

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:37.010
"Jean finds him there because what's happening
to her is making her do destructive things,

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.450
and she doesn't know why…

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:42.570
She feels he alone can give her answers because
he's lived both sides.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:47.650
He's lost control and killed and hurt people,
some of whom he even loved, and yet he's also

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:51.070
found a measure of peace and that's what she's
searching for."

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.070
A major death

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:56.550
The character of Mystique has been a part
of X-Men franchise lore since the very beginning.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:00.950
In the first film trilogy, she was played
by Rebecca Romijn, and was firmly on the side

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:01.950
of Magneto.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:06.920
But X-Men: First Class took the character
in a different direction, and drafted in Jennifer

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:07.920
Lawrence to play her.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.360
"I prefer the real Raven."

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.590
Instead of starting off as a villain, this
new Mystique was established as a young woman

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:21.310
who grew up with Charles Xavier as his adoptive
sister.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:25.860
Throughout the ensuing films in the new series,
her loyalties have shifted, but by the end

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:30.970
of Apocalypse she was back on Xavier's side,
helping to train young recruits like Cyclops

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:32.110
and Jean Grey.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.650
Now, with Dark Phoenix, it's time for her
to go.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:39.790
Mystique's death in the Dark Phoenix was revealed
early in the film's trailers, as a way of

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.860
making it clear that Phoenix means business.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.770
Writer and director Simon Kinberg has said
of Mystique's death:

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:50.630
"It's a movie where shocking things happen,
where intense, dramatic things happen.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.820
People don't just fall off buildings and dust
themselves off and walk away.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:58.870
There's a reality to this movie and a consequence
to this movie.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:04.610
Even more than that, it was to show that Jean/Dark
Phoenix is genuinely a threat to everyone,

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:05.730
including the X-Men."

